WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.617
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:05.917 --> 00:00:09.466
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.766 --> 00:00:15.832
Unit four: Subjunctive Mood. Today you will express demands and recommendations in formal English.

4
00:00:16.132 --> 00:00:18.726
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:22.853
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.717 --> 00:00:25.078
I suggest that.

7
00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:28.977
I suggest that means a frame that takes the base form.

8
00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:31.258
I suggest that he go home.

9
00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:34.549
Your turn. Say: I suggest that.

10
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.819
I suggest that.

11
00:00:39.583 --> 00:00:40.933
It is essential that.

12
00:00:41.917 --> 00:00:45.182
It is essential that means a formal frame for necessity.

13
00:00:45.783 --> 00:00:47.818
It is essential that she be present.

14
00:00:48.417 --> 00:00:51.545
Your turn. Say: It is essential that.

15
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.900
It is essential that.

16
00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:57.291
Were.

17
00:00:58.283 --> 00:01:00.979
Were means the subjunctive form for all persons.

18
00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:03.502
If I were you, I would wait.

19
00:01:04.117 --> 00:01:06.072
Your turn. Say: Were.

20
00:01:08.933 --> 00:01:09.772
Were.

21
00:01:10.517 --> 00:01:12.110
Hypothetical wish.

22
00:01:13.117 --> 00:01:16.904
Hypothetical wish means a wish about an unreal situation.

23
00:01:17.517 --> 00:01:19.040
I wish it were Friday.

24
00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:22.418
Your turn. Say: Hypothetical wish.

25
00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:26.755
Hypothetical wish.

26
00:01:27.517 --> 00:01:28.645
Formal demand.

27
00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:32.497
Formal demand means a strong, official request.

28
00:01:33.083 --> 00:01:34.735
A formal demand for change.

29
00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:38.165
Your turn. Say: Formal demand.

30
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.396
Formal demand.

31
00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:44.372
Recommendation.

32
00:01:45.383 --> 00:01:48.428
Recommendation means advice that something should be done.

33
00:01:49.017 --> 00:01:50.877
The report made a recommendation.

34
00:01:51.483 --> 00:01:53.985
Your turn. Say: Recommendation.

35
00:01:56.833 --> 00:01:58.009
Recommendation.

36
00:01:58.750 --> 00:01:59.705
Base form.

37
00:02:00.717 --> 00:02:03.390
Base form means the verb without -s or tense.

38
00:02:03.983 --> 00:02:06.389
Use the base form after suggest.

39
00:02:06.983 --> 00:02:09.601
Your turn. Say: Base form.

40
00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:13.746
Base form.

41
00:02:14.483 --> 00:02:15.566
Unreal.

42
00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:18.410
Unreal means not true now.

43
00:02:19.017 --> 00:02:20.610
An unreal situation.

44
00:02:21.217 --> 00:02:23.579
Your turn. Say: Unreal.

45
00:02:26.433 --> 00:02:27.539
Unreal.

46
00:02:28.333 --> 00:02:32.193
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:37.917
Visal, why do formal reports say I recommend that he be present, not that he is present?

48
00:02:39.017 --> 00:02:52.443
That is the subjunctive. After verbs of demand and recommendation, and after adjectives like essential, the verb takes its base form with no -s and no tense.

49
00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.120
Which verbs trigger it?

50
00:02:56.217 --> 00:03:09.202
Suggest, recommend, insist, demand, propose, require, and adjectives such as vital or important. Example: The committee demanded that the report be revised.

51
00:03:10.317 --> 00:03:11.980
And the other subjunctive?

52
00:03:13.083 --> 00:03:22.853
Were, as in If I were you, or I wish it were Friday. Were is used for every person in formal English to mark an unreal situation.

53
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.535
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:26.383 --> 00:03:31.854
Grammar focus: Subjunctive: verb of demand plus that plus subject plus base form.

55
00:03:32.154 --> 00:03:33.364
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.003
I recommend that he attend the meeting.

57
00:03:36.917 --> 00:03:38.893
It is essential that she be present.

58
00:03:39.783 --> 00:03:41.690
If I were you, I would wait.

59
00:03:42.633 --> 00:03:50.986
After suggest, recommend, demand or essential, use that + subject + base form. Use were for unreal situations with every person.

60
00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:54.960
Be careful! Don't say: I suggest that he goes.

61
00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:59.039
Say: I suggest that he go.

62
00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:00.793
Use the base form.

63
00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:04.368
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:06.528
The Committee's Demand.

65
00:04:06.828 --> 00:04:09.768
The committee demanded that the report be revised.

66
00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:13.370
It is essential that every member attend the meeting.

67
00:04:14.367 --> 00:04:16.668
I suggest that she consult an expert.

68
00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:20.409
If the budget were larger, the project would grow.

69
00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.444
The subjunctive keeps official language precise and formal.

70
00:04:25.533 --> 00:04:29.547
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:30.383 --> 00:04:32.302
I suggest that he blank early.

72
00:04:32.602 --> 00:04:35.686
A, leaves. B, leave. C, left.

73
00:04:39.233 --> 00:04:41.384
The answer is B: leave.

74
00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:44.457
It is vital that she blank present.

75
00:04:44.757 --> 00:04:47.586
A, be. B, is. C, are.

76
00:04:51.133 --> 00:04:52.854
The answer is A: be.

77
00:04:54.017 --> 00:04:55.714
If I blank you, I would wait.

78
00:04:56.014 --> 00:04:59.494
A, am. B, was. C, were.

79
00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:04.882
The answer is C: were.

80
00:05:06.017 --> 00:05:08.771
The subjunctive is typical of blank English.

81
00:05:09.071 --> 00:05:12.527
A, formal. B, slang. C, baby.

82
00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:18.020
The answer is A: formal.

83
00:05:19.183 --> 00:05:21.787
According to the reading, what was demanded?

84
00:05:22.087 --> 00:05:26.344
A, a revised report. B, more money. C, a new member.

85
00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:33.084
The answer is A: a revised report.

86
00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:37.568
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:38.417 --> 00:05:41.658
Write a sentence using the subjunctive after 'I recommend that...'

88
00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:51.788
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:52.088 --> 00:06:04.008
I recommend that every student read the instructions carefully. I also recommend that the teacher be available for questions. The verbs be and read stay in the base form after that.

90
00:06:04.308 --> 00:06:05.936
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:14.123
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and subjunctive: verb of demand plus that plus subject plus base form.

92
00:06:14.423 --> 00:06:19.374
Today's value is practical wisdom. Judge ideas by how well they work in real life.

93
00:06:19.674 --> 00:06:22.315
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

94
00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:26.196
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

